<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ilhéus</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as São Jorge dos Ilhéus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ilhéus is a port city in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahia">Bahia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, founded around 1536 as São Jorge dos Ilhéus, the seat of the hereditary Captaincy of Ilhéus. The colony struggled against indigenous attacks for two centuries. In the 19th and early 20th centuries it became the centre of Brazil's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cacao">cacao</a> boom, the world of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jorge-amado">Jorge Amado</a>'s novels.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ilheus.jpg" alt="Ilhéus" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Leandro M800 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Centro_de_Ilh%C3%A9us.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
